从某种程度上讲，每个编剧都可以被认为是一个悬疑编剧，因为明智地保留信息，直到适合揭晓的时机，这是叙事悬念和讲故事的重要组成部分，即使是一部文学小说之类的作品，也有极棒的反转。

00:24:39.519 --> 00:24:41.160
It's all mysteries and cliffhangers.
这全是谜团和悬念。

00:24:41.160 --> 00:24:45.200
Did you guys read Taffy's book, Long Island Compromise?
你们看过塔菲的书《长岛妥协》吗？

00:24:45.200 --> 00:24:46.359
No, I want to read that.
没有，我想读那本。

00:24:46.359 --> 00:24:58.779
There's such a good twist in there, such a good mystery twist that she reveals in the last couple pages that what really happened and it's just it's such a good reveal it's worth it's definitely worth reading.
里面有一个非常棒的反转，一个非常精彩的悬疑反转，她在最后几页揭晓了真正发生的事情，这个揭晓实在是太精彩了，绝对值得一读。

00:24:58.779 --> 00:25:07.119
Can I ask about the the the studio networks reaction to an unresolved sitcom episode?
我可以问一下，关于制片厂电视网对一集悬而未决的情景喜剧的反应吗？

00:25:07.119 --> 00:25:11.240
Did you did anyone say hey what the hell are you doing?
有没有人说过“嘿，你们到底在搞什么鬼？”

00:25:11.240 --> 00:25:25.488
I had one there was watching it back you know as we like like when I said I have notes like actually there's a few moments where it's like we could have made that cut a little bit you know I'm like looking at things that could have been a little different.
我回看的时候，你知道的，就像我说的我有做笔记，其实有几个瞬间觉得，我们当时本可以把那个剪得更紧凑一点，你知道的，我就是在看哪些地方本来可以处理得稍微不同。

00:25:25.488 --> 00:25:33.057
I felt like the crowd noise at the bar at the very end was where when the bar was empty it was like sounded like the bar was still full.
我觉得最后酒吧里的背景噪音，在酒吧空无一人的时候，听起来却好像酒吧里依然坐满了人。

00:25:33.057 --> 00:25:35.228
I would have tweaked that a little bit.
我本来会稍微调整一下那个部分。

00:25:35.228 --> 00:25:39.958
I remember at the time fighting this and 20 years haven't changed my opinion on this.
我记得当时就在为此抗争，而20年过去了，我的看法依然没有改变。

00:25:39.958 --> 00:25:54.039
I felt like them all eating the pineapple together at the end felt too, because I remember that that wasn't in the original script and that I remember that being added because I think there was like a studio note of some sort of like group all together.
我觉得最后他们一起吃菠萝的那个镜头显得太……因为我记得那并不在最初的剧本里，我记得那是后来加进去的，我想是因为当时收到了某种来自制片厂的意见，希望所有人能聚在一起。

00:25:54.039 --> 00:25:55.544
But Robert's really part of the group, right?
但罗伯特真的是这个团体的一部分吗？

00:25:55.544 --> 00:25:56.279
They're still friends.
他们还是朋友。

00:25:57.240 --> 00:25:58.307
I don't know.
我不知道。

00:25:58.307 --> 00:26:01.510
If I could just chop that out, I would.
如果我能直接把它剪掉，我会的。

00:26:01.510 --> 00:26:03.400
I sort of feel like it.
我有点这种感觉。

00:26:03.400 --> 00:26:03.960
I see that.
我明白那种感觉。

00:26:03.960 --> 00:26:11.880
And also, I feel like it deadened the uncertainty of where Ted and Robin are going to go next.
而且我觉得，这冲淡了泰德和罗宾接下来去向的不确定性。

00:26:11.880 --> 00:26:17.640
and that leads you into the limo episode where Robin is going off of someone else for New Year's Eve.
这也直接引出了加长轿车那一集，罗宾在跨年夜去和别人在一起了。

00:26:17.640 --> 00:26:19.116
I think it was a note card.
我觉得那是一个意见卡片上的要求。

00:26:19.116 --> 00:26:26.172
I think it was like, we still want to see, it's too early not to end on the gang being the gang and the note of Discord, I think.
我觉得就像是，我们依然想看到——在结局时如果不让这帮朋友还是这帮朋友，并且带有一点不和谐的音符，时间上还太早了，我是这么想的。

00:26:26.172 --> 00:26:28.359
I think there was some panic about that.
我觉得当时大家为此有些恐慌。

00:26:28.359 --> 00:26:30.908
We wanted to be like a group hug at the end.
我们当时想要的是最后来个集体拥抱。

00:26:30.908 --> 00:26:33.400
It's like, no, it's not a group hug moment.
结果发现，不，这根本不是一个需要集体拥抱的时刻。

00:26:33.400 --> 00:26:34.770
It also mystifies the pineapple.
这也把菠萝给搞得神神秘秘的。

00:26:34.770 --> 00:26:38.240
I feel like they just still be staring at that thing going It could be poisonous.
我觉得他们本来应该一直盯着那个东西，心想“它有毒吗？”

00:26:38.240 --> 00:26:39.240
It could be poisonous.
“它有毒吗？”

00:26:39.240 --> 00:26:40.240
It could be poisonous.
“它有毒吗？”

00:26:40.240 --> 00:26:41.240
It could be poisonous.
“它有毒吗？”

00:26:41.240 --> 00:26:42.240
Yeah.
对。

00:26:42.240 --> 00:26:43.240
Yeah, that's interesting.
对，这很有意思。

00:26:43.240 --> 00:26:54.880
It's an interesting thing, that tension, though, between the network and studio, which, I mean, this is a total cliche, but they are so afraid of people missing things and turning it off in frustration because they don't understand it.
电视网和制片厂之间的那种张力是一件很有意思的事，虽然这绝对是个老生常谈的话题，但他们真的太害怕观众错过细节，或者因为看不懂而沮丧地关掉电视了。

00:26:54.880 --> 00:27:05.400
So they value clarity in a way that I think writers like a little more gray and a little more obfuscation and you know what I mean?
所以他们极度重视清晰度，而在我看来，编剧们则更喜欢多一点灰色地带，多一点模糊处理，你知道我的意思吗？

00:27:05.400 --> 00:27:08.799
like less like they like to show not tell.
比如不那么直白，他们喜欢“用画面展现，而不是用语言说明”。

00:27:08.799 --> 00:27:21.039
But that's an interesting tension because I do know you guys have said and any of our lovely studio network executives who are listening that sometimes you get a network or studio note that actually saved you and was a great note.
但这种张力很有趣，因为我知道你们也说过，而且任何正在收听的我们可爱的制片厂和电视网高管们也会赞同，有时候你们收到的来自电视网或制片厂的意见确实能拯救你们，是个绝佳的建议。

00:27:21.039 --> 00:27:21.880
Tons of time, yeah.
有超级多的时候，是的。

00:27:21.880 --> 00:27:24.759
So many smart notes, yeah, we had a weird, great event show.
有那么多聪明的意见，对，我们曾有过一段奇妙且精彩的节目制作经历。

00:27:24.759 --> 00:27:25.599
Can't they give anybody?
难道他们就不能给任何人提吗？

00:27:25.599 --> 00:27:26.440
Yeah, I'm sure that.
对，我确信那……

00:27:26.440 --> 00:27:33.119
There was a premium at the beginning on the group has to seem happy and together and connected all the time.
在最开始的时候，有一个硬性要求，那就是这个团体必须时刻显得开心、团结且紧密相连。

00:27:33.119 --> 00:27:42.839
And I think we knew we were heading where this late season one discord and we knew we were heading towards some stuff that was gonna maybe be controversial with the studio network and it was, right?
我想我们当时就知道我们在走向第一季末尾的那种不和谐，我们也知道我们在朝着一些可能会引起制片厂和电视网争议的方向前进，事实也确实如此，对吧？

00:27:42.839 --> 00:27:44.759
Cardernally, it just was.
本质上，它就是这样。

00:27:44.759 --> 00:27:56.519
We got some pushback on some of the dramatic stuff we did at the end of season one and only over several seasons of us kind of proving ourselves and then realizing like this is actually a superpower of the show.
我们在第一季末尾做的一些戏剧化处理确实遭到了一些阻力，但经过好几季我们不断的证明，他们才意识到，这其实是这部剧的超能力。

00:27:56.519 --> 00:27:57.640
It's not a flaw of the show.
这不是这部剧的缺点。

00:27:57.640 --> 00:28:01.720
It's good that this show does kind of soap opera if you will or emo.
这部剧能搞点肥皂剧式的狗血或者说情感戏，这是一件好事。

00:28:01.720 --> 00:28:05.099
It's what distinguished the show from every other show.
正是这一点让这部剧与众不同。

00:28:05.099 --> 00:28:08.299
It is, and once they got that, we didn't get that note anymore.
确实如此，一旦他们理解了这一点，我们就再也没有收到过那种意见了。

00:28:08.299 --> 00:28:36.347
It was also, it was such a pivot point for all of television and the way people watch television because it was just a couple of years before, like DVDs were new and it was a couple of years before streaming and we like, especially CBS, there was no, they certainly did not want us to think of this show as each episode as a chapter in a book, you know, they wanted to think of it as like, each episode is a little, like a short story.
而且这也是整个电视界以及人们观看电视方式的一个巨大转折点，因为就在这之前的短短几年里，DVD才刚刚出现，流媒体也才刚出现几年，我们当时——尤其是CBS，绝对没有、也绝对不希望我们把这部剧的每一集看作是一本书里的一个章节，你知道的，他们希望我们把每一集看作是一个个小故事。

00:28:36.347 --> 00:28:42.859
They want to each one to be its own short story that's like the boss of chocolate, that's what it is.
他们希望每一集都是一个独立的小故事，就像什锦巧克力一样，就是那种感觉。

00:28:42.859 --> 00:28:49.508
But also, I mean, a lot of times you develop your voice or your creativity through that tension, right?
但同时，我的意思是，很多时候你正是在这种张力中培养出自己的声音或创造力的，对吧？

00:28:49.508 --> 00:28:53.317
Because like I said, this is, this is a standalone episode.
因为就像我说的，这是一集独立的故事。

00:28:53.317 --> 00:28:59.449
You could tune into this not knowing these characters and you could figure it out very quickly.
你不需要认识这些角色就能收看这一集，而且你能非常快地看懂。

00:28:59.449 --> 00:29:07.260
The world of it, the alliances, who was, but again, it was season, it forwarded the plot of the season all the same time.
它的世界观、人物关系、谁和谁是一伙的，但话又说回来，它同时也推进了这一季的主线剧情。

00:29:07.259 --> 00:29:17.059
And I think that there probably was, you know, there's a great Leonard Bernstein quote and something like, how do you create a work of genius?
我想当时可能也有——莱昂纳德·伯恩斯坦说过一句很棒的名言，大意是这样的：如何创作出一件天才之作？

00:29:17.059 --> 00:29:20.420
He said, you need a good idea and not quite enough time.
他说，你需要一个好点子，以及刚刚不够用的时间。

00:29:20.420 --> 00:29:24.420
And I think like, there's something about creative tension and limitation.
所以我觉得，某种程度上这就是创作张力和局限性的魅力所在。

00:29:24.420 --> 00:29:31.500
I know from directing independent films like, oh, we're being kicked out of this bar, we had five shots left, we only have one shot, what are we gonna do?
我从导演独立电影的经验中知道，比如，哦，我们要被赶出这个酒吧了，我们只剩五个镜头了，我们只有一个镜头了，我们该怎么办？

00:29:31.500 --> 00:29:32.339
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

00:29:32.339 --> 00:29:34.579
And that happened unhappy, thank you more please.
结果还挺开心的，谢谢，再来点。

00:29:34.579 --> 00:29:40.779
And my AD came up with this shot that is actually one of my favorite shots in the movie, because I think it's really elegant storytelling.
然后我的副导演想出了这个镜头，其实这也是我电影中最喜欢的镜头之一，因为我觉得这是一种非常优雅的叙事方式。

00:29:40.779 --> 00:29:49.019
So sometimes these limitations or these barriers or they force you into creative thinking.
所以有时这些限制、这些壁垒，会逼着你去进行创造性思考。

00:29:49.019 --> 00:29:58.900
And I feel like you guys in trying to, in being so young and in wanting to be deferential to these people who are writing your checks and allowing your show to be on the air.
我觉得你们在试图……因为太年轻，又想对那些写支票、允许你们的节目播出的人保持顺从。

00:29:58.900 --> 00:30:05.420
But you also had to subvert a lot of their notes and smuggle in stuff that, you know what I'm saying?
但你们同时也得颠覆他们的大量意见，暗中塞进一些私货，你知道我在说什么吗？

00:30:05.420 --> 00:30:07.420
There was a really interesting creative tension going on.
当时存在一种非常有趣的创作张力。

00:30:07.420 --> 00:30:17.380
I think we were trojan horsing, is that the vermin looking for a trojan horsing and some weirdness into what looked to be a traditional sitcom and that was there was tension to that at times.
我觉得我们是在用特洛伊木马战术……是不是那个虫子想找特洛伊木马战术，把一些古怪的东西塞进看似传统的的情景喜剧里，有时这之间是存在张力的。

00:30:17.380 --> 00:30:18.220
There was tension.
确实有张力。

00:30:18.220 --> 00:30:19.380
For sure.
