She got what we were going for.
她get到了我们的意图。

00:44:29.219 --> 00:44:30.420
So, yeah.
所以，是的。

00:44:30.420 --> 00:44:41.119
Well, in some ways, I mean, you can retrofit the pineapple into the larger story, which I think that, like you guys said, you were figuring out the show as you went.
嗯，从某种程度上说，我的意思是，你可以把菠萝的故事放到更大的叙事背景中去，就像你们所说的那样，你们是一边拍一边摸索这部剧的。

00:44:41.119 --> 00:44:53.820
And I think you were also getting bolder about taking bigger swings as the season went on, as the networking studio gave you a longer leash kind of like, let you do it, you know, more and and trusted your guy's vision.
而且我认为随着第一季的推进，你们也变得更大胆了，敢于做更大的尝试，随着电视网和制片厂对你们放宽了限制，有点像是让你们放手去做，你知道的，更多地信任你们的愿景。

00:44:53.820 --> 00:45:05.500
But I do think in how I met your mother verse, you could make an argument that, I mean, certainly, mystery, the unknown, which Ted is so scared of.
但我确实认为，在《老爸老妈的浪漫史》的宇宙中，你可以提出这样一个观点，那就是，当然，神秘感、未知，这是泰德非常害怕的。

00:45:05.500 --> 00:45:13.340
And Barney, I mean, from a Lord of Darkness perspective, is more attracted to, but from a more chaos perspective.
而巴尼，我的意思是，从黑暗之王的角度来看，他反而更被其吸引，但更多是从混乱的角度。

00:45:13.940 --> 00:45:18.619
But there is, I think part of Ted's journey is he has to make peace with mystery.
不过我认为，泰德的成长旅程中有一部分是，他必须与神秘感和解。

00:45:18.619 --> 00:45:21.179
He has to make peace with the unknown.
他必须与未知和解。

00:45:21.179 --> 00:45:22.179
So there's this huge part.
所以有很大一部分。

00:45:22.179 --> 00:45:28.139
There's this kind of epic symbol of that sitting beside his bed one morning is almost like a wink from the universe.
这种史诗般的象征有一天早上就静静地放在他的床头，几乎就像是来自宇宙的一个眨眼。

00:45:28.139 --> 00:45:46.139
I know, I've always felt like the central tension of the show is that struggle between fate and self-determination, like even down to the title, how I met your mother, it sounds like it could be an instruction manual, like how to meet the love of your life.
我懂，我一直觉得这部剧的核心张力就是命运与自我决定之间的这种挣扎，甚至从剧名《老爸老妈的浪漫史》来看，它听起来就像一本使用手册，比如如何遇到你生命中的挚爱。

00:45:46.139 --> 00:45:48.739
As though that's something you can just go out and do.
就好像那是你只要走出去就能做到的事情。

00:45:48.739 --> 00:45:52.420
But in fact, it's like, it's really like, how this happened.
但事实上，这其实是，这更像是，这一切是如何发生的。

00:45:52.420 --> 00:45:56.739
How did that, how did, what, how did this happen to, for this to unfold?
怎么会这样，怎么会，什么，这一切究竟是怎么一步步发展成这样的？

00:45:56.739 --> 00:46:01.699
And also it occurs to me, Barney has all kinds of like systems and formulas.
而且我突然想到，巴尼有各种各样的系统和公式。

00:46:01.699 --> 00:46:04.219
He's trying to game the universe also.
他也是在试图搞定宇宙。

00:46:04.219 --> 00:46:05.059
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

00:46:05.059 --> 00:46:05.880
All the time.
无时无刻不在这么做。

00:46:05.880 --> 00:46:07.420
Even though he's a little more open to the unknown, but yeah.
尽管他对未知稍微开放一些，但确实如此。

00:46:07.420 --> 00:46:09.099
Yes, but you cannot make it happen.
是的，但你无法强求它发生。

00:46:09.099 --> 00:46:16.980
You have to, you have to embrace that part of life that is just gonna deliver things to your doorstep and you make with them what you will.
你必须，你必须拥抱生活中的那一部分，它只会把事情送到你的门前，然后你用它们来成就你想做的事。

00:46:16.980 --> 00:46:17.820
Yeah.
对。

00:46:17.820 --> 00:46:39.179
But I think that that's part of the starting the show when they're 27, is like, your 20s or so confusing and you've been liberated from a system where, especially if you did college and maybe even grad school, like you're liberated from the system that's very ordered and regimented and you know where you have to be when and you have your meals here.
但我觉得这也是27岁开始拍这部剧的一部分意义所在，就像你的20多岁是如此迷茫，你刚从一个体制中解放出来，特别是如果你读过大学甚至研究生，你会从那个非常有序、充满常规、你知道什么时候该在哪里、在哪里吃饭的体制中解放出来。

00:46:39.179 --> 00:46:49.496
And then you're thrust out into the world and you just have to make sense of the chaos of like being young and in New York City and not having a ton of money and not knowing who you're going to marry and where you're going to live.
然后你被推向世界，你必须去理清那种年轻并在纽约生活的混乱感，没有多少钱，不知道你要和谁结婚，不知道你要住在哪里。

00:46:49.496 --> 00:46:51.059
And like, there's so many unknowns.
而且，有太多的未知数。

00:46:51.059 --> 00:46:52.000
And I agree.
我完全同意。

00:46:52.000 --> 00:47:07.520
I mean, I think it's a story about many things, but one of them is about a young man who has to accept mystery in his life and the wisdom of the unknown, that there's actually something guiding him.
我的意思是，我认为这是一个关于很多事情的故事，但其中之一就是关于一个年轻人，他必须接受生活中的神秘感和未知的智慧，事实上冥冥之中有什么在指引着他。

00:47:07.520 --> 00:47:16.300
I mean, if he'd married Stella, if she'd shown up at the altar, like He'd be divorced now, you know what I mean?
我是说，如果他跟斯特拉结婚了，如果她出现在圣坛前，就像……他现在早就离婚了，你知道我的意思吗？

00:47:16.300 --> 00:47:20.179
Like there were things that would not have worked.
有些事情就是行不通的。

00:47:20.179 --> 00:47:25.559
So he was actually, what looked like heartache was actually him being protected on some level.
所以实际上，那些看似心碎的经历，在某种程度上其实是对他的保护。

00:47:25.559 --> 00:47:30.000
So maybe them eating the pineapple was them internalizing and ingesting that mystery.
所以也许他们吃掉那个菠萝，就是他们在内化和吸收那种神秘感。

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:32.840
Maybe it was genius that they could find it right now.
也许他们能马上找到它，简直是天才般的安排。

